<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Gdpr's cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project for the strongest form
    of the consumer-in-Base test there is: Base does not merely *call* this section, it
    *implements* its contract. IUserDataContributor is the Article 15 fan-out seam that
    every service owning user-scoped tables must implement, so a Contracts/ *folder*
    inside Humans.Gdpr would make Base reference a section and cycle
    (memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    Everything here is named from outside:
      - IUserDataContributor + UserDataSlice + GdprExportSections — the contributor half,
        named by every service that implements it.
      - IGdprExportService + GdprExport — the orchestrator half, named by Users'
        ProfileController (the /Profile export download) and by this section's own
        GuestDataController.
    Nothing else is public: the fan-out service itself is internal.

    References only the Interfaces slice of Base — the bottom of the graph. IFanout and
    IOrchestrator live there (in the Humans.Base.Interfaces namespace, which is why the
    interface files here carry a using for it).
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Base\Humans.Base.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
